          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-monad"} lax-idempotent 2-monad
            or pseudo 2-monad on a 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            a pseudo
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/left+adjoint"} left adjoint
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : T A \to A
            to the unit
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                    %mo :
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \eta_A : A \to T A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            %strong
              continuous
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : T A \to A
            has a further left adjoint, forming an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
          %p
            Note that every free
            = succeed "-algebra" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T B
            is continuous: it is a property of lax-idempotent 2-monads that the multiplication
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi μ
                    %mi B
                  %mo :
                  %mi T
                  %mi T
                  %mi B
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mu_B:T T B \to T B
            has left adjoint
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\eta_B
          %p
            For the rest of this page we will say “
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            \-algebra” to mean “pseudo
            = succeed "-algebra\u201D." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi Ind
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A = Ind(A)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ind-completion"} ind-completion
                monad on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimits"} filtered colimits
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+category"} continuous category
            %li
              %p
                Specializing the previous example, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                      %mo =
                      %mi Idl
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A = Idl(A)
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
                completion monad on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poset"} Poset
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/directed+joins"} directed joins
                = succeed "-algebra" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+poset"} continuous poset
          %p
            Note also that if an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor+theorem"} adjoint functor theorem
            applies (such as if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A
            are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattices"} complete lattices
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+presentable+categories"} locally presentable categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is continuous if and only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A \to A
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/continuous+functor"} continuous functor
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For instance, if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is the downset monad on
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Poset"} Poset
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suplattices"} suplattices
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+completely+distributive+lattices"} constructive completely distributive lattices
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/axiom+of+choice"} axiom of choice
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+distributive+lattices"} completely distributive lattices
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#WoodFawcett"} WoodFawcett
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is the free small-cocompletion monad on
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Cat
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocomplete+categories"} cocomplete categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/completely+distributive+categories"} completely distributive categories
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+category"} presheaf category
                “monad”, whose “algebras” are
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+categories"} total categories
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/totally+distributive+categories"} totally distributive categories
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+cocompletion"} free cocompletion
                monad under coproducts, then continuous algebras are “locally connected” in a sense: the extra left adjoint
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo →
                      %mi T
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to T A
                decomposes every object as a coproduct of connected ones.
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is a “filter monad” on topological spaces, which can be regarded as a “presheaf category” type construction with topological spaces thought of as
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+multicategories"} generalized multicategories
                (specifically, as
                = succeed ")," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relational+beta-modules"} relational beta-modules
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed ")." do
                  %a{:href => "#Hofmann"} Hofmann
          %h2#characterizations Characterizations
          #Retract.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Consider the following conditions on a
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %ol
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a continuous algebra.
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
                sub-
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                \-algebra of a free
                = succeed "-algebra." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
                is a retract (up to isomorphism) of a free
                = succeed "-algebra." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              Then (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              (3), and both converses hold if idempotent 2-cells split in the underlying 2-category.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              This is B1.1.15 in the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a : T A \to A
              has a left adjoint
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℓ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \dashv a
              is an adjunction in the 2-category of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "-morphism)." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⊣
                    %msub
                      %mi η
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a\dashv \eta_A
              is an isomorphism, the unit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℓ
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \dashv a
              is an isomorphism, by the theorem on
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "adjoint+triple#FullyFaithFulAdjointTriples"} fully faithful adjoint triples
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              (2), and (2)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⇒
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Rightarrow
              (3) is obvious. For the converse, see the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elephant"} Elephant
          #Comonadicity.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              be the pseudo
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-comonad"} 2-comonad
              on the 2-category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              is lax-idempotent, and a
              = succeed "-algebra" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is continuous if and only if it is a
              = succeed "-coalgebra." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Lax-idempotence of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              follows from the fact that the adjunction
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⇄
                    %mi T
                    %mi Alg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \rightleftarrows T Alg
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-adjunction"} lax-idempotent 2-adjunction
              = succeed "-coalgebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G A \to A
              has a left adjoint in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T A \to A
              of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is lax-idempotent, any left adjoint between
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              = succeed "-morphism." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            This theorem is proven in (
            %a{:href => "#Kock"}> Kock
            ) in the special case when the base 2-category is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%281%2C2%29-category"} (1,2)-category
            (the result is due to
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bart+Jacobs"} Bart Jacobs
          %h2#related_pages Related pages
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-monad"} lax-idempotent 2-monad
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
          %h2#references References
          %ul#WoodFawcett
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Wood"} Richard Wood
              and Barry Fawcett, “Constructive complete distributivity. I”. Math. Proc. Camb. Phil. Soc. (1990), 107, 81
          %ul#Kock
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Anders+Kock"}> Anders Kock
              , “Monads for which structures are adjoint to units”, JPAA 104 (1992).
          %ul#Hofmann
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dirk+Hofmann"}> Dirk Hofmann
              , “Duality for distributive spaces”. Theory Appl. Categ. 28 (3) (2013), 66–122,
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "http://sweet.ua.pt/dirk/"} web site
